/-!
# Identifying the original reduced moved module

The literal join of V_v and [R₂(G_v),L_v] has centralizer R_v inside
C_LT(v). Its L_v-image is the original A₆ quotient, with a two-group
quotient over that image. Thompson generation supplies an FF witness;
the complete B.5 classification makes its moved space Irr⁺. Both original
subgroups are nontrivial and generated by their own L_v-commutators.
Their inclusions into the common module therefore identify them.

Under L_v=K_v this commutator is normal in G_v, contradicting the proved
nonnormality of the original V_v at the preferred escaping point. Combining
both Thompson cases proves strict residual enlargement there. Component
recognition, blocks, splitting and fixed-space elimination remain open.
T-invariance and TI retain producer qt-d-1222-source and final discharge
owner qt-d-12634-source.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith,12.6.11 and B.5.1/6, printed pp.825,99--105.
-/

public section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Representation Representation.BinaryOffender Stellmacher
